        {
          "id": 612195828,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "test/captures/netperfmeter.pcapng.gz contains a NetPerfMeter packet trace using port 9000 for NetPerfMeter over TCP. The S101 dissector assumes all TCP port 9000 packets to be S101 messages and labels them accordingly, even if there is no S101 header. So, NetPerfMeter with this MR but without this commit shows these packets as \"NetPerfMeter/S101\", which would be wrong.\n\nWithout this MR, i.e. the current upstream/master, the label is simply \"NetPerfMeter\", i.e. the wrong S101 just gets overwritten. So, this fix makes sure that the packets are correctly labelled as \"NetPerfMeter/TCP\". Since the test suite suite_netperfmeter.py checks that the label is correct (i.e. \"NetPerfMeter/TCP\" and not \"NetPerfMeter/S101\"), this fix is necessary for this MR.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5649708,
            "username": "dreibh",
            "public_email": "dreibh@simula.no",
            "name": "Thomas Dreibholz",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b2cd008b76724c78722d428c7836d7a098cbae94d69faf8142e43fc2445bec17?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/dreibh"
          },
