      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 613126623,
          "type": null,
          "body": "So this proves that the option to stash commits locally and change the commit message does not work as expected, and that we should ask the author to stash before merge... The commit message should have been:\n```\nNetPerfMeter: protocol column display improvement\n\nAppend protocol name \"NetPerfMeter\" with col_append_sep_fstr(), instead of\noverwriting the underlying Transport Layer protocol name.\n```\nInstead of two separate commits",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
